WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:09.080
Now, if you are doing software development or you are working with data projects and of course it depends

00:09.080 --> 00:14.680
on your role in the projects, there will be many different types of tasks and activities that should

00:14.680 --> 00:16.040
be done in the projects, like.

00:16.040 --> 00:22.480
There will be a lot of brainstorming about new ideas and coding solutions, debugging, generating documentations,

00:22.600 --> 00:27.080
discussing the different types of architecture, doing root cause analysis.

00:27.200 --> 00:31.840
So the spectrum of activities and tasks in each projects usually is very huge.

00:31.880 --> 00:38.040
And of course we can go and use the help of different AI tools to assist us with those tasks and activities.

00:38.040 --> 00:41.680
And there is like not one AI tool that can cover all those stuff.

00:41.840 --> 00:45.160
I tend to jump between Copilots and something like ChatGPT.

00:45.200 --> 00:49.400
Okay, so now I'm going to go and map those different tasks to either ChatGPT or copilot.

00:49.440 --> 00:51.040
So now let's focus on the ChatGPT.

00:51.200 --> 00:54.320
The first one is brainstorming and ideas.

00:54.320 --> 00:59.200
So now if we have in our project a big task or let's say a big issue, that we want to find a solution

00:59.200 --> 00:59.760
for it.

00:59.760 --> 01:05.800
I tend to use of course, tools like ChatGPT in order to have a discussion about the topic, in order

01:05.800 --> 01:10.580
to explore and discuss multiple ideas and then start evaluating all those ideas.

01:10.580 --> 01:14.500
The next one where I found myself using GPT is doing the project planning.

01:14.620 --> 01:16.620
So it is as well something high level.

01:16.620 --> 01:22.100
You can go and discuss with the ChatGPT about the design of your project, and you can as well discuss

01:22.100 --> 01:24.620
the milestones, the roadmap of the projects.

01:24.620 --> 01:29.780
The next thing that I find myself using ChatGPT is for learning, knowledge and research.

01:29.780 --> 01:34.620
If you are working with big data projects, you will be overwhelmed with the amount of cloud services

01:34.780 --> 01:36.900
and AI analytics tools.

01:36.900 --> 01:37.060
So.

01:37.100 --> 01:42.300
And of course you can go and learn new stuff, gather information and knowledge using ChatGPT.

01:42.340 --> 01:45.660
Okay, moving on to the next task we have generating documentations.

01:45.660 --> 01:50.420
Writing documentations is always a painful process and consumes a lot of time.

01:50.420 --> 01:54.420
And I tend to use tools like ChatGPT in order to generate those documentations.

01:54.420 --> 01:57.620
But of course I always review the documentations and make it short.

01:57.660 --> 02:01.940
Okay, moving on to another topic where I use ChatGPT is that to discuss architecture?

02:01.980 --> 02:06.660
Of course, if you are starting new projects, there will be like different types of architecture in

02:06.660 --> 02:08.060
order to implement the projects.

02:08.060 --> 02:11.890
And of course you can discuss with the ChatGPT about the different types of architecture.

02:11.890 --> 02:16.690
And if you give the specifications about your projects, then you can discuss with the ChatGPT which

02:16.730 --> 02:19.170
architecture is suitable for the project.

02:19.170 --> 02:25.090
And another task that I find myself always like researching is exploring the best practices, tips and

02:25.090 --> 02:29.370
tricks so you can have a discussion with the ChatGPT about the recommendations.

02:29.370 --> 02:30.970
What are the best practices?

02:31.090 --> 02:32.650
What are the common pitfalls?

02:32.650 --> 02:38.450
In order to make sure that your code and your solution is always up to date with the best practices?

02:38.450 --> 02:43.810
And one more thing if there is like in the project, a very complex task, then I tend to have a discussion

02:43.810 --> 02:45.050
with the two like ChatGPT.

02:45.170 --> 02:50.730
In order to break this complex task into small pieces and start finding the solution for each piece.

02:50.770 --> 02:55.170
And now, in the other hand, I'm using copilot in order to solve different type of tasks.

02:55.170 --> 02:57.530
So here where I get my hands dirty in the code.

02:57.530 --> 03:03.610
So while I'm coding, I'm using full time copilot in order to assist me because it provides directly

03:03.610 --> 03:09.050
inline suggestions and help me to code faster and reduce the human error that I might make.

03:09.050 --> 03:14.770
So while I'm writing a code or debugging, I tend to use Copilot, and I don't find myself going to

03:14.810 --> 03:17.710
ChatGPT to ask about code or syntax.

03:17.710 --> 03:19.750
We can do it directly in the copilot.

03:19.750 --> 03:24.150
And one task that is very famous in any software development we have the refactoring.

03:24.150 --> 03:29.030
So if you have like a code that is slow and bad designed and you want to refactor the whole code, you

03:29.030 --> 03:33.750
can do it directly in your code together with the copilot in order to find optimizations.

03:33.750 --> 03:37.070
And I use as well copilot in order to add inline comments.

03:37.070 --> 03:41.350
So I don't find myself going to ChatGPT and asking to add comments to my code.

03:41.350 --> 03:44.550
You can do it directly in your code using copilot.

03:44.550 --> 03:48.790
And of course, if everything is working perfectly, I have the best practices, the good performance,

03:48.790 --> 03:53.070
I have the comments, but still you have to maintain nice style and format of your code.

03:53.070 --> 03:55.710
And of course now we can do that directly using the copilot.

03:55.710 --> 03:59.230
We don't have to go and jump to ChatGPT in order to style and format your code.

03:59.230 --> 04:02.870
And as you can see, I'm currently using both of them for different types of tasks.

04:02.870 --> 04:07.310
So again, if I have the feeling that I have to discuss something, I go to ChatGPT.

04:07.390 --> 04:14.190
But once the idea is very clear and I know the solution, then I start using copilot in order to write

04:14.190 --> 04:19.630
the code and with the help of the copilot, I can deliver clean and professional codes.

04:19.630 --> 04:23.230
So this is how I currently use both ChatGPT and Copilot.
